# 90% CL upper limit on the DM-electron reference cross section sigma_e from DarkSide-50
# (liquid argon, 12306 kg d, 4-170 electrons), heavy mediator (F_DM = 1): arXiv:2207.11968, PRL 130, 101002
# (2023). Argon ionization form factors of arXiv:1802.06998 (RHF bound states, continuum in the hydrogenic
# potential with Z_eff: the same W_1 tables and binding energies as lib/atomic_responses/*/Ar_<shell>.txt),
# standard halo of arXiv:2105.00599 (rho = 0.3 GeV/cm^3). No numerical release: digitized from the solid red
# curve of Fig. 2 (top left) of the arXiv source (fig2_limits.png, 3324x3776 px; axes calibrated on the major
# ticks, curve = centre of the red line in each pixel column), resampled in log mass. Within 10% (on average 3%
# above) of the DarkSide-50 curve of the XENONnT S2-only paper (arXiv:2601.11296, Fig. 4(d), 34 MeV - 1 GeV).
